<%
/*
  SPEC §4's memo, as a template (TICKET-0024, D-2).

  Everything here is a loop or a substitution. There is no LLM in this stage
  (CLAUDE.md invariant 3) and — deliberately — no decision either: which
  sections exist, which bullets survived the caps, which dimension decided the
  call and what would upgrade a Watch are all fields on the `Analysis`, computed
  by `src/analyse/derive.ts`. If something you want to change here needs an
  `if` with a judgement in it, the change belongs in stage 2.

  `it` is the view model from `src/memo/render.ts`:
    it.analysis    the Analysis, verbatim
    it.header      { name, call, score, coverage, url, one_liner, status_reason }
    it.label(ids)  evidence ids as "[E1][E2]" — memo-local labels
    it.sources     [{ label, id, url, retrieved, type }] in first-cited order

  Edit freely: a partner changing the layout of a memo should not have to read
  TypeScript. Two things are load-bearing rather than cosmetic — every bullet
  prints `it.label(...)` beside it, and the sources table prints every row.
  Dropping either breaks the citation guarantee (ADR-0003), not just the look.

  Blank lines are normalised by the renderer, so a stray one here is not a diff
  in the output.
*/
%># <%= it.header.name %> — <%= it.header.call %> · score <%= it.header.score %>/100 · coverage <%= it.header.coverage %>%

<%= it.header.url %><% if (it.header.one_liner) { %> · <%= it.header.one_liner %><% } %>
<% if (it.header.status_reason) { %>
_Partial reading: <%= it.header.status_reason %>_
<% } %>
## Why this call

<% it.analysis.why_this_call.forEach(function (bullet) { %><%= bullet.text %><%= it.label(bullet.evidence_ids) %> <% }) %>
<% if (it.analysis.upgrade_trigger) { %>
**To upgrade this Watch:** <%= it.analysis.upgrade_trigger %>
<% } %>
<% it.analysis.sections.forEach(function (section) { %>
## <%= section.heading %>

<% section.bullets.forEach(function (bullet) { %>- <%= bullet.text %><%= it.label(bullet.evidence_ids) %>
<% }) %><% if (section.omitted > 0) { %>
_<%= section.omitted %> further observation(s) in the analysis, not shown here._
<% } %><% }) %>
<% if (it.analysis.what_would_change_my_mind.length > 0) { %>
## What would change my mind

<% it.analysis.what_would_change_my_mind.forEach(function (bullet) { %>- <%= bullet.text %><%= it.label(bullet.evidence_ids) %>
<% }) %><% } %>
<% if (it.analysis.unknowns.length > 0) { %>
## What we could not verify

<% it.analysis.unknowns.forEach(function (unknown) { %>- <%= unknown %>
<% }) %><% } %>
## Sources

| id | url | retrieved | type |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
<% it.sources.forEach(function (source) { %>| <%= source.label %> (`<%= source.id %>`) | <%= source.url %> | <%= source.retrieved %> | <%= source.type %> |
<% }) %>
